APPLE IIGSIMAGEWRITER LQ DRIVERTESTINGCURRENT AND PREVIOUS RELEASE NOTESBEN KONING-----For easiest testing on the system disk, rename the file"ImageWriter.LQ.Dxx" to "ImageWriter.LQ" while transferring from theMacintosh to the Apple IIGS into the */SYSTEM/DRIVERS directory.  Thisway you don't have to modify the "AT ImageWriter LQ" CDEV.The PRINTER and MODEM port drivers had a bug which caused the LQ driverto print garbage on certain occasions (when $89 or $09 sent to portdriver by printer driver).  Please install the new versions in theDRIVERS directory.The PRINTER and MODEM port drivers have been modified to be capable oftrue 19.2K baud output rates.  Running the LQ at 19.2K baud will nowresult in a 75% speed improvement over 9600 baud, unlike before. The PRINTER and MODEM port driver have been modified so that responseis much quicker if the printer is unconnected.-----System Disk 6.0 ships here.F49		8-Jan-92Removed WaitCursor/InitCursor calls from status message routines.  Most applicationsput up their own (wait) cursors anyway, and our WaitCursor call was causing problemswith applications such as HyperCard which do cursor animation with hi-bit-setcursor record pointers.F48		10-Dec-91Paper sizes for International A4 and International Fanfold changed as per customerrequest: X size increased from 132 to 136 80-dpi-pixels.  Untested.F47		4-Dec-91Radio button hit area is now set to 0,0 so that it's set correctly by the toolbox.F46		15-Nov-91PrJobDialog dialog box line edit field tabbing now works right.F45		23-Aug-91Set language to American upon s_reset (ESC c); fixes bug where setting non-Americansettings for the language-select DIP switches would cause incorrect text modeoperation with nonmapped characters.Now storing zeros in our-picframe X1 and Y1 before we allow the user-supplied rect(if any) to be copied in.  Retrofix bug fix from SW driver.F44		20-Jun-91Changed back to say "Rendering page image" because Bob didn't like it the other way.F43		19-Jun-91Cosmetics: changed line edit box sizes and saying "Rasterizing page image".If bit 15 of wDev is set to 1 (by app) then during-printing status box won't show.F42		15-Apr-91Incremented version number to 4.2.Job dialog box no longer updates twice when first drawn.  Style dialog stillredraws twice because of its funky portrait/landscape controls, however.Command-Period works (as well as ESC) as key-equivalent for Cancel in bothSetup and Job dialog boxes.Saved code space by converting NotCorrectDevDialog to AlertWindow usage.Saved code space by converting CheckAndDoAboutBox to AlertWindow usage.Saved code space by using WaitUntil in ShowPrinterErrorStatus routine.System Disk 5.0.4 ships here.F41		2-Dec-90 6:30pmThe printer communication error (IW) and resending of imager-call-band(LQ) is happening when it shouldn't.  Probably bug in appletalk PAPcode; "fixed" by calling PrDevStatus (PAPStatus) a second time if a toolerror occurred.  In other words, PAPStatus, is returning an error($805-Name Not Found) and when it's called immediately after, it returnsno error.  This bug manifests itself by resending a band of graphicsdata or by displaying printer communications error message whileprinting draft/text mode.F40		30-Nov-90 7:15pmModification to end of CloseDoc code to ensure that the SpoolFinishGETis always called if there is a print loop error, to ensure that spoolmemory or files are deallocated/removed (note that unique printerconnection is not an issue here since the printer connection open/closeis all in PicFile).Lost sync bug determined to be in and fixed in AppleShare FST.F39		28-Nov-90 2:20pmMade network spooling work correctly; lost sync bug still exists.F38		27-Nov-90TJ089 bug remains an issue, presumably SpoolPut lost sync.Added code so that if spooling-to-disk happens while the boot volume isappleshare, the TMP.XXXX file gets written out to the appropriate USERdirectory.Added error passing around PutGetExit in printloop's GetPic/PutPicbottleprocs so that QD is better notified upon SpoolGet error.F37		24-Nov-90Added space on either side of slash which divides the printer drivername and the port driver name at the top of both dialog boxes.Crashing bug was found to be bank-wrap-around problem in ROM 3 QDcursor handling code.F36		19-Nov-90We discovered that the latest crashing bug is caused by two things:1) QDaux has a problem with running out of memory during the DrawPictureprocess: it has an internal stack imbalance problem and crashes.  Thishas been fixed in 6.0.  We need to put in this change--only--for 5.0.4.2) In the IW and in the LQ drivers, we were not checking for tool errorafter drawpicture; now, if tool error after DrawPicture, the PrPicFiletool error is set, the print loop error (PrError) is set, and we exit.F35		13-Nov-90Changed version ID from 4.0 to 4.1.In SpoolPut, there was no error checking on the SetHandleSize call (werelied on the RealFreeMem call just above)!  "BCS PutNoMoreMemory" addedjust after SetHandleSize (found by Mensch).5.0.3 System Disk shipped around 1-Nov-90.F34		13-Aug-90Text-mode font mapping now handles case where GetTextSize call returnsa zero.  Fixes "Nexus" application quirk.B33		9-Aug-90Upon the PrDevWrite call, we don't treat $08FF as an error, because itcould be simply PAP saying that the printer's appletalk buffer is full.Fixes Iduna choking after several cards bug.B32		18-Jul-90OpenDoc no longer saves individual values from the print recordthat are needed by OpenPage/ClosePage--it saves the value of the user'sprint record handle instead.  Fix for apps which modify rPage and otherfields between OpenDoc and OpenPage.  Impact on testing is on manualfeed, idleproc, number of copies, and page range correctness.B31		30-Jun-90Added field to print record "wResScaling" at printX+20 ($78 absolute)offset in the print record.  The wResScaling is a constant whichdescribes how much this printer driver scales up the image (just priorto scaled-down printing at finer dot pitch) in order to obtain higherresolution.  This field has been added for the application's information.It always has a constant value of 3 for the ImageWriter LQ.Job Dialog user interface line edit box fix:  Wherever the line editcursor is blinking, no matter in which of the 3 boxes, typing ispossible, even if a non-line edit control was just selected.  Fixed byremoving ParamWordA-flag restriction in ConductJobDialog; the LE handlethat is kept around is now always valid.No changes to color/density dither pattern handling in Standard modeat this time.  Unlike the IW driver, this remains at 80 hdpi.  This isa policy decision.  We can either take the fast mode out or make itanother option in one of the two dialog boxes.  Std-640-red comes outok in my tests, but then again, the dither pattern is very coarse so ared object with some kind of pattern may get cancelled out.B30		25-Jun-90The self-ID code is now takes advantage of the network PrDevStatus(PAPStatus) call if possible.  Responsiveness improvement for thePrGetPrinterSpecs call and PrJobDialog.  Appletalk error handling needsto be retested.B29		20-Jun-90Changed names of quality modes to the following: Text Only,Standard, and Best.In 320 mode+Black/White, the color saturation is no longer doubled.It was previously being doubled in *all* cases (to increase colorsaturation), but this would cause black/white images to look too dense.Test case: DeluxePaint/King Tut Black/White+Standard.In PrOpenPage, we forgot to skip over the OpenPicture call and therelated spool-beginning code just above it if in Text/Draft mode.Therefore, spooling memory as well as a picture handle was createdinadvertently if in Draft/Text mode.  Fixed by adding some newbranching at end of OpenPage and at beginning of ClosePage code, as wellas change in order of first two things at beginning of CloseDoc code,so that dialog is removed *after* if-draft-PrinterClose code.B28		6-Jun-90Fixed PutText text-mode recording bottleproc so that a text stringbeginning at a coordinate that is outside the current clipping regionis not recorded and hence not printed during ClosePage.  Preventsdrawing-on-second-page DrawPlus bug and Iduna text-at-bottom bug.B27		1-Jun-90The PRINTER and MODEM port driver have been modified so that responseis much quicker if the printer is unconnected.Inside PrClosePage is the ClosePicture call.  If this call returns anerror, as it would if our bottleprocs failed (due to full disk duringspooling-to-disk, etc) during page data recording, that error is nowreturned out of the PrClosePage call as a tool error.Iduna's command-period abort was not working.  After the imaging routinecall (during which the IdleProc runs) we now check the print looperror (PrError/PrSetError) status.  It was already being done at thebeginning of each sheet; now it is done after every imager call.AppleTalk error message handling needs retesting!The 8K RGB to KCMY conversion table is no longer used in the originalsense.  A conversion lookup table is now used, which is parallel instructure to the standard 16 16-entry color palettes table.  Onlythose color palettes which are referenced by an SCB are calculated.Result: less time spent (no delay after "Positioning print head"anymore) and about a 7.4K reduction in memory footprint.A much smaller direct-page stack frame is used for the GetPic/PutPicbottleprocs, as per suggestion by Mensch.  This may or may not haveany effect on low-memory bugs, but makes for better coding practice.The code in source file "imager.aii" has been made more readable.B26		14-May-90NOTE: Many of these retrofit changes, induced by the debugging processof the new IW driver, will have to be tested rigorously before thisdriver graduates from beta status.New label sizes added for 3.5" and 5.25" floppy disks, with 1/4 gapsin between the labels.  Gap-size needs to be fixed in IW driver.We're now remembering the handle from the OpenPicture call in theOpenPage routine and passing it to KillPicture in the ClosePageroutine.  We were leaving one small handle per page around!Small, dormant bug fix: imager.aii/"its_intl": doing AND #$FF afterlongm just before add to "lang_tbl" base address; garbage could havebeen in upper accumulator.Potentially serious dormant bug fix: PiFiCalcBandPasses: PiFiLast-BandHeight could be zero and would be *used* as such if the wanted-bandsize is an even multiple (no remainder).  Fixed by preinitializingPiFiLastBandHeight to the band buffer height and modifying it only ifthere was a nonzero remainder from the divide.  Thus it is always atrue indicator the last band's height, in all situations.In metrics.aii/GetQuality, if our internal wQuality field in theprint record is set to Better but the wDev Better bit is unasserted,then we force our wQuality field to Standard.  Thus the wDev Betterbit is now tracked truly, either way.B25		4-May-90Selecting land+vc+bett+manual feed would cause crash.  Crash was in_NoteAlert, because in PrPicFile's setbufdims code, we blindly set thenumber of horizontal bytes to our bandbuffer locinfo's number ofscanline bytes.  During landscape printing, our bandbuffer is very talland skinny--a small number of horizontal scanline bytes, thus messingquickdraw functions other than our imaging up very badly.  Fixed byensuring that PrPicFile's setbufdims code can only make the qd bufdimsbigger, and never smaller.B24		3-May-90Added "Allocating imaging memory" status message.Removed two cases of CheckHandle in entry code.Interchanged paper types for European B5 and International Fanfold.The IntlFanFold is now (correctly) type=3, and European B5 is type=4.Changed label "ChunkSize" to "OutputFlowQuantum".Text-mode bug fix: cmp #$20 for control chars couldn't work becauseof garbage in high 8 bits of long accumulator.Text-mode bug fix: garbage in high 8 bits of long accumulator nearimager text-mode section to select one of the built-in fonts.Text-mode bug fix: there was a word-store to "n_textfont", whichis a byte.  Must be retrofitted to IW.Spooler now uses GS/OS calls and RealFreeMem; changed itsfine-tuning equates.Some of the low-memory "fixes" from the new IW driver have beenincorporated: 1) Removed MaxBlock check-after-NewHandle in picfileband malloc code; 2) Added RealFreeMem check before NewHandle inpicfile band malloc code; 3) 1.25X BufDims text height and 1X portloc info width.B23		12-Apr-90Space Improvement #2: Building RGB to KCMY conversion lookup table atruntime; saves 8K (on disk only).Superior "Lwht" landscape white elimination speed improvement, whichoperates even on head scan bands which are partially filled (speed#9).Changed "50% Vertical Size" to "Vertical Condense".Light-yellow-640 not showing up bug has been fixed for both portraitand landscape (actually, in landscape the bug didn't manifest itselffor the LQ, but it was still there).B22		19-Mar-90Job Dialog From/To box interpretation has been improved.  All previouserror checking still exists, plus it's now possible to fill-in only onebox and have the results come out as expected.  For example, selecting"From: 5" and leaving "To:" blank will cause printing from 5..doclength.Likewise, one could fill-in only "To: 8", leaving "From:" blank, forexample, thus causing only pages 1..8 to be printed.B21		7-Mar-90During out of memory conditions, the proper error ($0201) is nowalways returned."Black & White" has been renamed to "Black/White" to be consistentwith new ImageWriter driver in the PrJobDialog box.Update events are now handled properly.  Was causing problems withwindoid-using processes such as Video Keyboards.B20		27-Feb-90If text/draft mode selected, the following metrics settings are nowreset to their default values: 100%, VertGap, Darker, Bidirectional,Portrait.  The others are left alone, since text mode can deal suc-cessfully with different paper sizes and 50% vertical condense.B19		22-Feb-90The horizontal dialog box line code has been changed to not rely onthe underline of the Shaston 8 font; about box now uses StaticTextcentering.  Dialogs look better in TopDraw, which doen't use Shaston 8.Attempt at producing better colors in Better mode resulted inrealization that it'll be very hard to do since 640-mode is dithered.This causes 640-mode colors which are dithered with black to producea pure black RGB->CMY dot on the paper right next to a bright CMY dot;the pure black just kills the color.  Could be fixed by taking two640-mode pixels into account at a time when calculating the CMY color.Might be an improvement for later system disk release.Text/draft-mode horizontal positioning has been fine-tuned slightly.There are still possibilities for overlap.About-box has been changed slightly.Changed code around SetBufDims call in PrPicFile.  MultiScribeGS on a1M machine now prints, but it still hangs afterwards.A18		16-Feb-90		Pre-BetaDraft/text-mode horizontal positioning bugs fixed.  The wrong print-headposition command was being used and was being executed after thehorizontal-spacing-for-the-native-font-select command was issued, thusrendering its results random.  There is still some overlapping, whichcan perhaps be fixed by some tedious fine-tuning.A17		15-Feb-90		Pre-BetaThe lost-data-under-MultiScribe-landscape-33-labels bug is actually aMultiScribe bug, provable by running with the test "iwlq.ms.bug" driver.MultiScribe is not recording any picture elements into page two.Large Oval/RoundRect vertical (with Better mode) clipping bug seemsto have gone away.  Don't know why; could be due to 5.0.3d3 or to fixfor 0-length-spool-requests in A16 release.Spooling cases for to-disk only and to-memory-with-tiny-blocks haveboth been tested.  Spooling now back to normal (to-memory 5K blocksuntil it runs out (<128K maxblock), then to disk).  Needs testing withhuge documents under low memory conditions.  Also, PrPicFile-low-memory-error-return is set for maxblock <32K.Sheet feeder has been made slightly more reliable.  The command to usea new bin is issued only if it differed from the last time.Changed Job dialog text to reflect the fact that the sheet feederselection pertains to the current PAGE, not the current COPY.  SelectingBin 2 on a one-page document and asking for 15 copies results in 15sheets being pulled from Bin 2, for example.  But a two-page documentcould have all of its 15 copies of its first page come from Bin 2, andall of its 15 second pages from Bin 3, for example.Job dialog box LineEdit boxes ("Copies", "From", and "To") were fixeda long time ago to be very robust... except checking for 0.  Fixed.Different and wierd number entries in these boxes needs retesting.Got rid of need to use source file "m16.portdriver".Text (draft) mode 2nd page text string in DrawPlus is application-related and not a driver bug.A16		12-Feb-90		Pre-BetaForced spooling-to-disk remains in place for test purposes.Fixed bug in spool routines so as to handle zero-length getpic/putpicrequests.  Caused AppleWorksGS to say abort printing after just one pagewhen spooling to disk.  Modified spool routines to use GetTick insteadof QD Random for the random filename suffix.Careless tiny bug introduced in last release fixed.  InIdleProcAbortErrCheck, on direct connect port driver would store toPrError.A15		12-Feb-90		Pre-BetaTo test spooling performance, spooling to disk has been forced, justfor this release.Fixed bug in ID string interpretation routine.  Apparently there areseveral different versions of the LQ firmare out.  Changed device-notlq status alert box a little bit since it is called now wheneversomething's not right, like out-of-paper, etc, at Job dialog time.Fixed bug where (network) LQ with sheet feeder got confused aboutpaper height (unnecessary top-of-form commands in FF len set code).Added a status message about rendering current page image (displayedduring call to DrawPicture).Added a "Cancel" item to the manual sheet feed dialog box.  Works forboth draft/nondraft, with "Cancelling" in status box for draft modedelay problem where the app still has to go through its printing-loop.Status message handling is more robust.  On the network, the out-of-paper, select-is-off, etc., work better now.  Added "printer is in use"status message upon someone else using printer; also, the note alert(which already exists for non-LQ-connected situations) is put up uponJob dialog with busy printer rather than hanging until the other usersare done.  However, interrupting a job in the middle of a page stillcauses repeating data to be sent.A14		2-Feb-90	Not Yet Beta CandidateThe makefile has been changed to not do beep/duplicateiigs duringofficial builds.  The output file "ImageWriter.LQ" now appears at thetop level of the directory.Status box text says "Recording picture data" and starts out with"Preparing to record data" during the printing loop.The way in which the 100/66/33% reduction values are encoded in theprint record's wDev location has been changed to remain compatible withthose applications which modify wDev themselves.  Internally, the0..2 coding for 100/66/33% still holds, however.  Also, the GetConvert-QualBits routine has been redone.  Fixes DesignerPrints bug.A would-be bug has been detected theoretically which could have causedstepping on memory.  In several places where a NewHandle memory requestsize is being calculated, the size requested is too small because ofnatural number/counting number confusion (ie, if y2-y1=N, alloc N+1 !!).The memory-left-limits for banding buffer allocation and spool-to-diskthreshold-defaults have been distinguished from one another.  The bandbuffer alloc out-of-memory error remains at MaxBlock result < 32K, whilethe spool-to-disk-default has been increased to go to disk if Maxblockresult < 100K.  Both of these can now be independently changed for easyperformance tuning.For Iduna, the Change-A-Range-Of-SCB-Values (ChSCB) PicComment has beenimplemented and superficially tested.  This PicComment, together withthe Change-Color-Table-Entry (ChCTBL) PicComment already implemented,allow the application full control over colors everywhere in thedocument to be recorded ("spooled") and printed.The ChSCB PicComment changes have exposed two bugs in the Landscapespeed improvement #6 qualification code.  Fixed.A metrics bug caused 66% DrawPicture scaling to be too small.  Ithas been fixed without re-introducing the 66%-imaging-too-much/big-using 2-pages when 1-page needed bug.  CalcMetrics now causes 100/66/33to create 1/1.5/3 times printable area to apps while two new routines(ConvertImgToRPage/ConvertRPageToImg) do 100/66/33 3/2/1 times scalingif Better is selected.  Should fix test matrix bug #79, #167? andmaybe others.Dither patterns have been improved for 320-mode/Standard (If IW & 320then colortemp*2).  Has drawback of maxing out on dark colors.  MakesIW-mode graphics look much less infantile because only the denser halfof the pattern table is used.A13		12-Jan-90Speed Improvement #5 has been implemented (no big deal).  It is activewhenever Portrait is selected, standard color tables/scb's are used,hscaling=1 (which happens during Better/any% or during Standard/33%),and 640 mode only.  It speeds up black/white-only imaging by at least10% (not really enough to be noticable).A waiting-to-happen-but-unerupted bug has been found and fixed in thecolor table pure white scanning loop for speed#3.Speed Improvement #6 has been implemented.  Whitespace elimination inlandscape modes with significant restrictions.  Great speed improvementfor all-white lines (columns) (but not partial-white (like portraitwhite elimination)).						D12		8-Dec-89The Paper Type popup menu in the _PrStlDialog call was displayinginverse-question-mark characters while in AppleWorksGS.  We wererelying on $E7 character being a narrow space character.  Fixed,though the menu items don't line up as nicely.A dialog appears for if something other than an ImageWriter LQ isconnected instead of just doing a SysBeep.  This is checked for atPrJobDialog time just before the job box appears.Sheets-Left-To-Print message in the status box during printing wouldnot work correctly when printing a multi-copy, multi-page document(incorrect logic to do sheets*pages each time, so now there is adecrementing counter that's initialized to sheets*pages).  Fixed.PrPixelMap call has been given a quick test, a bug was fixed, and nowseems to work correctly.  This call is not made by many applications.A PicComment end-of-page marker handling bug has been fixed, eventhough it "worked", that is, multipage documents could be printedcorrectly, albeit for the wrong reason (the PicComment routine wasnot exiting with A=0/c=0 and thus THAT was terminating the DrawPictureprocess, and not the code in GetPic which checked the end-of-page flag,even though that code actually never checked the flag anyway!  Every-thing is now completely fixed).  Multipage and multicopy documentprinting needs to be tested VERY thorougly.Fixed dispatch code bug (entry.aii); the last call in the list(_PrGetPgOrientation) was incorrectly considered illegal and causeda planned breakpoint (BRK #$BB) to occur.Draft vertical positioning has been improved: no matter what thevertical condense setting, the Y coordinates are always correct fortext all the way down the page.If banding buffer size exactly equalled the imaging size (a possiblebut uncommon occurrence), nothing would be printed (PiFiLastBandHeight,which would be 0, would be used to adjust the last band even if therewas only one band).  Symptom: DrawPlus, Land, No Gaps, Color.Picture,my particular system/memory configuration would just recalibrate theprinter, do all sheets-left-to-print box messages, and exit withoutprinting.  Fixed.Medley didn't seem to want to print multipage documents.  Fixed bychanging code in the two places where we set the clip regions to rPagesize instead of screen-sized default to use SetRectRgn for settingthe visrgn instead of just setting it to the same handle as the cliprgn.Other programs are apparently unaffected, either way.The bits in the wDev field of the print record listed below use reverselogic; a "1" setting indicates a default setting rather than a "0".We were using positive logic when setting/reading these.  This didn'tcause any problems except for those few applications which read/writethese bits themselves, such as Medley and Iduna.  The driver is nowcompatible with the accepted way of handling these bits (although in-ternally, 0 still means portrait rather than landscape, etc.).  Thebits with reverse logic are (see GS Toolbox Reference I-15-13):	print record.wdev.Bit 1	Orientation		0=land	1=port (default)	print record.wdev.Bit 2	Vert Condense	0=cond	1=norm (default)	print record.wdev.Bit 6	Vert Page Gap	0=no 	1=yes  (default)	The PicComment (for end-of-page mark and new stuff) handling has beenmade more robust by checking for a signature and version number.  Seethe README file for specific information.The _PrPicFile routine is now sensitive to a certain PicComment typewhich allows mid-document color changes.  See the README file forspecific information (this has been done for Iduna).	D11		22-Nov-89The vertical line feed (LF) spacing is now reset to default 6 lines/inch,as a courtesy to older applications using the printer after the driveris done with it (page length and TOF was already being reset).At PrJobDialog time, we now check if the device connected is reallyan ImageWriter LQ.  If not, then SysBeep and exit with error ($1308pntrConFailed).Major PrJobDialog text and formatting changes; minor PrStlDialog textand formatting changes.D10		20-Nov-89Trivial white space elimination algorithm has been installed, effectivefor all portrait modes.  Major speed improvement, especially forsparsely dirtied areas of pages, especially for Better mode.QuickDraw wasn't informed of the need for larger clipping buffers, byusing the SetBufDims call.  Fixed.  HodgePodge/Picture windows, paintapplications, and others using PPToPort don't crash anymore in Bettermode.Faster quality mode has been eliminated as a choice for the user.  Ifuser choices permit, however, the ImageWriterII output mode is stillinvoked, thus keeping the tremendous speed gain.1/4" Vertical page gaps were not produced properly.  An application'sprintout would start right at the top edge of the paper, even if theno-vertical-page-gaps option was off.  Fixed.Formfeed now works correctly regardless of the paper type installed.This means that Option-Period abort will eject even legal, envelopes,etc., correctly.  It also means that very diverse types of pin-fedpaper can be printed correctly.  For example, one can select a mailinglabel paper type, draw the label in an application, and the number ofcopies selected will be the number of labels printed out.  This didnot work correctly in the older printer drivers.Page breaks in applications would always be one line off.  Fixed.DrawPlus would not line up lines inscribed within ovals or rects.Discovered to be DrawPlus bug; DTS notified.Many new diverse paper types have been added to the paper type popup,including several wide paper sizes to take advantage of the widecarriage and labels and envelopes to take advantage of the new betterformfeed handling.Internal band buffer allocation changed so that very small paper typessuch as labels can be used (doesn't start out dividing band memory bytwo; does align-24 first).When the Print Job dialog box appears, the Copies line edit box isactive.  Immediately typing a number will cause the number and inser-tion point cursor to appear in the Copies box.TAB now moves cursor from "From" to "To" line edit box in Job dialog.If "From" > "To" in Job dialog, the two values are exchanged.  Also,range checking is now more robust.The OpenPage call now always leaves the current GrafPort set to the"printing" (spool recording) GrafPort.  The OpenDoc call also does this,but some applications apparently change the GrafPort between the OpenDocand OpenPage calls.  For example, selecting From=2, To=3 in the Jobdialog and then printing a 4-page document from Writer's Choice Elitecaused garbage on the screen from the rendering of the unprintedpages 1 and 4.The PrPicFile call now handles zero-length spool recordings correctly.This means, for example, that specifying a page range from 3 to 5 whenthere is only 1 page in the document won't cause problems.D9		13-Oct-89Added "B5 Letter" (176x250 mm) to "Paper Type" menu, upon noticing itin the toolbox reference manual.  Was easy to add; the more the merrier.Fixed freezing-in-Medley bug.  Also found serious bug in Medley, whichis being fixed by the author.  Medley wasn't looking at "iDev" in theprint record correctly (2 means LQ; it was doing cmp for non-1).  Also,the "crWidth" field in the print record now always has the value of 960,since several apps seem to expect that value.  The real, dynamic carriagewidth value, which the driver needs for internal purposes, is now storedelsewhere in the print record.Fixed no-printing-in-DeluxePaintII bug.  It was expecting a copy of the"prInfo" subrecord of the print record in "prInfoPT" (which it shouldnot do, but I'm not using that space anyway).  A copy of those 14 bytesis now maintained there.Next release next week.  Priorities, in order: Paint programs/HodgePodgepicture window crashing (QD bug); Stepping on memory (if that's thecase); Speed improvement #3 (the final frontier in performance); Issuesresultant from matrix; Other QD bugs causing anomalies in Better mode.D8		6-Oct-89Many bugs are still under investigation; the driver won't be analpha candidate again until next release (next week).A bug (in QuickDraw) has been found whenever any app uses PPToPortinside its printing loop.  Bad news for HodgePodge pictures and paintapplications, which will crash.Spooling/Banding buffer memory problems (when apps just bail andrefuse to print at all) have yet to be addressed.Medley still freezes on page setup dialog.No more data is being lost on Multiscribe/land/66/"megafont".  I wasdoing metrics scaling *2 when I should have been doing *3/2 inGetImagingSize.  However, it's still feeding an unneeded empty page.Several bugs fixed for draft mode (imager now doesn't ever do posnanymore on null string; imager now outputs CR at end of every string).This shouldn't fix the last-line-in-drawplustest-draft-mode bug,however.A tiny bug in the run-length-encoding scheme (posn+1) is fixed.Graphics would appear horizontally misaligned.When manual page feed was selected, its dialog would appear at wrongtimes (jsr -> brl in PrinterFormFeed).  Fixed.D7		29-Sep-89Metrics code has undergone some major revisions.  All metrics bugsever detected must be retested.  Also, because run-length-encoding ofprinter-ready output is now implemented, be on the lookout for smallglitches around the edges of solid graphics.All metrics code is now contained in the source file "metrics.aii";no more metrics-like code in "printloop.aii".  Metrics code has beengreatly simplified and sanitized; no more voodoo code exists.Whenever a reduction-type of option is selected in the Page Setupdialog, such as 33% or Std.Point Size, the application should see agreater document area.  That was fixed last time.  But, in addition,this larger document area is now imaged and printed and may nowbe used.  Thus, the bug where the third "!" wasn't showing up inthe DrawPlus document "drawplus.test" on landscape or 33%, etc., isfixed.The lost-data-bug in landscape/no-page-gaps with "drawplus.test", dueto one of the fallacies in the old metrics code, is fixed.Run-length encoding has been implemented at the output of the imager,just before the data is sent to the printer.  Instead of merely sendinga single command to print graphics followed by the graphics data foran entire head scan, the data is broken up into chunks of zero, nonzerorepeating, and nonzero nonrepeating wire-strike groups, and the 'LQ'spositioning, print-repeating-graphics, and print-non-repeating-graphicscommands are issued accordingly.  This has resulted in an average 2-3Xspeed improvement in all nondraft quality modes.Currently being addressed: Memory problems (where it doesn't print atall), any other metrics problems, and then another speed improvement(caching of calculation results or trivial-blanks elimination whileimaging from off-screen pixels to printer-pixels).D6		15-Sep-89Several remaining metrics bugs have been fixed.  These were all dueto the fact that (possibly) incorrect data was returned in the rPage,rPaper, iHVRes, and crWidth fields in the print record, in conjunctionwith Reduction settings and/or Landscape.  An application knows howbig a page is in inches by doing rPage divided by iHVRes.  If adocument is created that fills the entire 8x10.5" of a USLetter, forexample, and then the user selects Landscape mode, then that documentmust be printed on two pages.  That part was correct.  But select areduction size, like 33%, and that document is still printed to twopages because the rPaper, etc., data structures weren't being changed(nor should they really be...).  So the bug fix is as follows:  Selecting33% or 66% (or Standard Point Size) really increases the bigness of the"paper" to be printed on, and this can be noticed by the fact that thescroll bar thumbs get smaller in an application such as DrawPlus.  Yes,the ImageWriterII driver works this way as well.Thus, BRC # 52033, 52034, 52035 are claimed to be fixed.A potentially serious problem exists in that I could not get Medley 1.1to work (it froze).  I will speak with Eric Soldan (author) about thisto see what the problem is (it IS an 'LQ driver problem).Any remaining metrics bugs (such as the Medley problem) now have highestpriority.  Otherwise, I will be implementing the 2X speed improvement.D5		8-Sep-89Sheet feeder usage in conjunction with appletalk was not working verywell due to the peculiar way in which the 'LQ's appletalk firmwarereports page empty status when a sheet feeder is installed.  Ithas been worked around in a compromising sort of way.Too many form feeds were happening at end of print job.  Fixed.This bug was related to a wrong policy decision last release withrespect to the "No Gaps" option.  Currently, form feed happensat the end of all sheets ("sheets" means pages and/or copies), butonly if the "No Gaps" option is disabled.  Form feed also alwayshappens upon command-period user-interrupt.  Form feed will nothappen anymore in any other case.The "crWidth" field in the print record is now being set correctly.Last release it was accidentally being set to 1/2 the required value,causing artifacts such as landscape printing not being right-justifiedon the page.Coming up:  Run-length encoding analysis of imaged data in an attemptto exploit the 'LQ's "print repeating graphics columns" command;nominal speed improvement will be around 2X in all nondraft modes.D4		1-Sep-89Part of the code related to Draft Mode (the stdText quickdrawbottleproc) was carelessly overwriting an internal data structure.Draft mode font mapping needs to be retested.The CompactMem call has been taken out of the spooler initializationcall.  This was causing HodgePodge to crash.  This is really a Hodge-Podge bug (select font: Shaston 3; print draft; select other font;system will crash next mousedown in menu bar); but I'm not sure ifCompactMem should have been called by me anyway.Standard Point Size (alias V.Condense) now causes the application toknow about the entire page (ie, it's now possible to print a page fullof text, rather than only being able to use 1/2 the page).The source compiles with the latest official DSG equates.Blank horizontal bands/image-part skipping is fixed (BRC # 52036).Formfeed now happens on command-period even if in one of the non-draftprint quality modes.Formfeed happens appropriately at end of print job even if "No VerticalGaps" is enabled.Much code has been cleaned up.Serious problems still exist in metrics, manifested particularly byfeeding extra sheets of paper (now even on all-default print options),left-edge clipping on landscape, incorrect right-edge positioning onlandscape.  Also, the linker decided to make the driver 10K too big.In addition, cut sheet feeder selection doesn't work over appletalk.D3		25-Aug-89Draft mode international characters needs to be tested very thoroughly,both over direct connect and appletalk.  Lines should be writtenstarting and/or ending and/or mixed with international characters.BRC # 52029 (0's preceding text) is fixed.  BRC # 52030 (incorrectdraft mode (horizontal) positioning) is greatly improved for now; thefinal word on this is kind of a policy decision.BRC # 52031 (landscape draft prints as portrait) will never really befixed.  Landscape draft mode won't be supported.  The main problem isto figure out a way to do this: ie, should the the Portrait icon beautomatically hilited when the user selected draft mode?  But thenwhat about other features that might cause certain modes to havedifferent effects, such as selecting Faster and then printing in, say,33% reduction (causing it to print as Standard because Faster onlysupports 320/640/Std.PointSize options)?  Some thinking has to be doneabout these issues.With the new MODEM and PRINTER printer port drivers installed, all bugswhich deal with garbage being printed should be fixed.  This includesBRC # 52032, 52036, 52037 and just maybe even parts of BRC # 52033,52034, 52035.These last three bugs, plus other that I know of, are the result ofmetrics bugs (the rPage/rPaper/iHRes/iVRes fields of the print recordaren't being set correctly depending on chosen paper type, etc).  Thisis the next area of concentration; after that, several bugs related toprinted images not being scaled correctly will be investigated.D2		18-Aug-89BRC # 52038 and 52032 are claimed to be fixed. A new, much better README file has been written.  Also, most of thisweek was spent doing a print spooler feasability investigation.A dispatch table bug has been fixed (if an application made aPrGetPgOrientation call it would never have worked).A new, much faster printing mode has been added.  It is called "Faster"in the Print Quality menu.  The old "Faster" mode is now called"Standard".In the print record (test this!), a new field has been defined (thisis in the new README file): wQuality, at printX+16, or $74 offset fromthe start of the print record.  Its values are 0=Draft, 1=Faster, 2=Standard, 3=Better.  The old print quality indicators (the BetterText bit in the wDev field in the print record and the bJDocLoop bytefield in the print record) should still always remain valid, however(test this).  The purpose of adding the new field is becaue the new"Faster" mode setting needs to be remembered by the print record.The new Faster mode operates the ImageWriter LQ just as if it werean ImageWriter II.  Since it is nearly impossible to get the metricsright otherwise, the only non-default print options are 320/640 modeand vertical condense ("Standard Point Size").  If you tried to printin Faster mode, say, with 66% reduction, or in Landscape, etc., thedocument will print as if Standard mode were selected.The new Faster mode prints lighter.  When the Darker option is selected,it will be darker--as dark as the Standard mode.No new features will be added after this release!  This (limited)feature was added solely due to its great speed performance advantage.D1		7-Aug-89All memory allocation (NewHandle) calls use user-id of type $10xx.This number can be changed with an equate in the source.AppleTalk is supported.AppleTalk error messages are supported, with Apple-Period Quit stillworking even while error condition.Apple-Period works in addition to IdleProc.  This goes againstdocumentation, but this way is better.Draft mode font sizes/styles/types are considered while selecting anative IW LQ font.  Underline and Boldface work as expected; Times,Courier, and Shaston are assigned special native LQ fonts; pointsizes over 14 yield double-wide print; point sizes less than 8 yieldsuper-small print.Draft mode international characters (accented letters, etc) work.Not all international characters are supported by the LQ; therefore,some map to spaces, others to the same character without the accentmark.Lots and lots of internal code cleanup.Draft mode speed improvement to recover speed lost by adding of inter-national character feature above.  Printing international mixed withnormal characters needs to be tested thoroughly.D0		17-Jul-89First release of ImageWriter LQ driver to testing.  Pre-Alpha stage;fully functional in the application interface but lacking severalfeatures (appletalk with error recovery is the main one), containingbugs mostly due to integration of features, and lacking severalperformance improvement enhancements.